.TH PERFEKTBLUE 1 "June 2026" "PerfektBlue 2.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
perfektblue \- Bluetooth-first adaptive security assessment framework
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B perfektblue
[\fIGLOBAL OPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
PerfektBlue discovers Bluetooth devices through BlueZ D-Bus, records evidence, matches target
profiles, builds a compatible assessment plan, and produces evidence-backed reports.
.PP
The default risk policy is passive. Active verification requires a target-specific module,
compatible profile, sufficient confidence, written authorization, and explicit command options.
.PP
Running
.B perfektblue
without a command opens the interactive Bluetooth intelligence console.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B menu
Open the interactive terminal workspace with target, session, and safety context.
.TP
.B doctor
Check Linux, Python dependencies, BlueZ access, and Bluetooth adapters.
.TP
.B adapters
List Bluetooth adapters.
.TP
.B discover
Discover Classic Bluetooth and BLE devices.
.TP
.B fingerprint TARGET
Rank target profiles and explain their confidence.
.TP
.B plan TARGET
Show selected and skipped assessment modules.
.TP
.B assess [TARGET]
Run the generated assessment plan and store a session.
.TP
.B report SESSION
Generate a JSON or standalone HTML report.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-backend bluez|simulated
Select live BlueZ or the deterministic simulator.
.TP
.B \-\-risk passive|active-safe|lab-active
Set the maximum permitted module risk.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine-readable JSON.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/perfektblue/config.toml
User configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/perfektblue/
Session database and artifacts.
.SH SAFETY
Use only on systems you own or are explicitly authorized to assess. A blocked, unsupported,
inconclusive, or no-known-path result does not prove immunity to unknown vulnerabilities.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bluetoothctl (1),
.BR btmon (1)
